      "section": "What I’m watching",
      "category": "video",
      "title": "Wild Tales",
      "creator": "Pedro Almodóvar",
      "note": ". This was recommended to me by a Colombian friend, as I wanted to [resurrect my Spanish](https://tim.blog/2007/09/20/how-to-resurrect-your-high-school-spanish-or-any-language-plus-be-on-the-cbs-early-show/?utm_source=convertkit&utm_medium=convertkit&utm_campaign=5bf) prior to a trip to South America. It’s gorgeously shot, impeccably directed, and it will make you laugh and cringe in equal measure. Here’s the description: “\\[An\\] award-winning anthology from Argentina composed of six short films united by a common theme of tragedy, revenge, and violence found in everyday detail. Nominated for 2015 Best Foreign Language Film Oscar.” You can find the trailer [here](https://youtu.be/Utq0aDEp084?si=Kcjc4JBjKdoYMGSr).",
